{"name":"Maroon Light","hex":"#bf3160","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"maroon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An escaped black slave of the Caribbean and the Americas or a descendant of such a person. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A castaway; a person who has been marooned (abandoned)."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Associated with Maroon culture, communities or peoples."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/maroon"},{"term":"light","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye (about 400–750 nanometers): visible light.","Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye or in nearby ranges (infrared or ultraviolet radiation)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To start (a fire).","To set fire to; to set burning."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/light"}],"entries":[{"title":"Maroon","blocks":[{"text":"Maroon is a brownish red color that takes its name from the French word marron, meaning chestnut. Marron is also one of the French translations for \"brown\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Textile_LACMA_M.55.12.27.jpg/330px-Textile_LACMA_M.55.12.27.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maroon","wikidata":"Q25393814"},{"title":"Light","blocks":[{"text":"Light, visible light, or visible radiation is electromagnetic radiation that can be perceived by the human eye. Visible light spans the visible spectrum and is usually defined as having wavelengths in the range of 400–700 nanometers (nm), corresponding to frequencies of 750–420 terahertz. The visible band sits adjacent to the infrared and the ultraviolet, called collectively optical radiation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Prism_flat_rainbow_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Prism_flat_rainb